Provenance
----------

This software is a clean-room implementation. Its knowledge of disc and image
formats derives solely from public documentation and standards (for example
ECMA-130 for the CD physical format) and from the observed behaviour of
hardware and of files supplied by the copyright holder. No third-party binary
has been disassembled, decompiled or otherwise reverse engineered in its
creation, and no third-party source code has been copied into it. See the
`docs/` directory, which records the derivation of each format.

Product names referenced in the documentation are used only to identify the
formats and behaviours described. They are the trade marks of their respective
owners, and no affiliation with or endorsement by those owners is claimed or
implied.

Copy protection
---------------

This software does not circumvent, and will not be extended to circumvent, any
effective technological measure protecting a copyright work. It reads
unencrypted media only. This is a deliberate and permanent limitation.

Third-party components
----------------------

This software targets the .NET platform (MIT licence, redistributed as part of
the self-contained runtime) and uses operating-system APIs (IMAPI2 and SPTI on
Windows; SG_IO on Linux) supplied with the operating system. It bundles no
other third-party code. External tools that DiscForge can launch are not part
of DiscForge, are never bundled with it, and remain subject to their own
licences.
